course: dictionary
lesson: 9433
title: Stage: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word stage has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one to use. «The class will perform a play on stage.» Here stage is the raised floor where actors stand, because the clues are perform and play.
explain: «Big rockets drop their empty stages to become lighter.» Here a stage is one part of a process. Ask: what word would fit? Try part in the sentence: «drop their empty parts to become lighter» still makes sense, so stage means part here.
explain: «At this stage in the story, the hero is alone.» Stage can also mean a point in the events or in growth. The words at this tell you where we are in the story. When you are unsure, swap in another word and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A stage can be a raised floor in a theatre or hall where people act, sing or speak.
fact: A stage can be one step or part of a process, such as the stages of a life cycle: egg, caterpillar, chrysalis, butterfly.
fact: To stage a play or event means to put it on for people to watch.
fact: «Actors in a play rely on each other's lines; if one forgets, the others are left stuck on stage.»
fact: Stage fright is the nervous feeling people can get before they perform in front of others.
exercise: «The class will perform a play on stage.» What does stage mean here? | A step in a process | * A raised floor where people act | To put on a show for people | A long, thin road
exercise: «Butterflies go through several stages, from egg to adult.» What does stages mean? | Very old things | Shows put on for people | * Steps or parts of growth | Raised floors in a theatre
exercise: «The teacher staged a play for the parents.» What does staged mean? | Hid from view | Forgot the words to | Divided into steps | * Put on for people to watch
test: «Big rockets drop their empty stages to become lighter.» What does stage mean? | A raised floor for actors | To put on a show | Something forgotten | * One part of a process
test: «At this stage, the story gets very exciting.» What does stage mean here? | A theatre floor | * A point in the events | To act on a stage | Something that drowns
exam: «Ella felt sick with stage fright before she went on stage.» What does stage fright mean? | Feeling very hungry | A wish to sleep | Fear of heights | * Nervous feeling before performing
